<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$85 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-Tenders total A$85 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three issuers came to the Australian commercial paper market on Tuesday for a total of A$85 million.</p>
<p>Locals General Property Trust and ICI Australia Ltd sold parcels of A$30 million and A$25 million respectively while McDonald's Corp issued A$30 million.</p>
<p>Discount securities traders said short end turnover was minimal with little interest in maturities beyond thirty days ahead of U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's economic outlook speech to the U.S. Senate Budget Committee at 1500 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;Everyone's heading back towards cash and 30 days and waiting,&quot; one Sydney-based dealer said.</p>
<p>At 11.30 a.m. (0030 GMT), March 90-day bank bill futures were trading at 94.37, down one point on the day.</p>
